# Files the Vercel build does not need. The build runs `npm run build`
# (tsc → vite build → scripts/prerender.mjs), so it needs index.html, src/,
# public/, scripts/, the tsconfigs and vite.config.ts — nothing else.
#
# Paths are anchored with a leading slash on purpose: an unanchored `supabase/`
# would also exclude src/integrations/supabase/, which the build imports.

# Local dependencies and build output (Vercel installs and builds its own)
node_modules
/dist

# Database SQL and documentation — reference material, never imported
/supabase/
/docs/
/README.md

# Local tooling state
/.claude/
/.vercel/
*.log

# Local environment files. Vercel injects each project's own environment
# variables into the build, and Vite gives real process env precedence over
# .env files — so uploading these would only risk one project's values (or a
# server-side secret) leaking into another project's build.
/.env
/.env.*
